body:
Based on the fork of @db48x from #661. Doesn’t support the ‘autogroup’ ACL functionality.

This ACL works for us (formatted slightly for readability)
```json
{
  "acls":[{
      "action":"accept",
      "src":["group:employees"],
      "dst":["tag:proxy:*"]
    }
  ],
  "hosts":{},
  "groups":{
    "group:employees":[
      "john.doe",
      "jane.doe"
    ],
    "group:proxy":[
      "mycorp"
    ]
  },
  "tagOwners":{
    "tag:proxy":[
      "group:proxy"
    ]
  },
  "ssh":[
    {
      "action":"check",
      "src":["group:employees"],
      "dst":["tag:proxy"],
      "users":["some-allowlisted-user"],
      "checkPeriod":"8h"
    }
  ],
  "disableIPv4":false,
  "randomizeClientPort":false
}
```

